  "question": {
    "text": "If mean of a poisson distribution of a random variable \\(X\\) is 2 , then the value of \\(P(X > 1.5)\\) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rifGI",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{3}{e^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u3YIL",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{3}{e}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "K0dji",
      "text": "\\(1-\\frac{3}{e}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jNFfP",
      "text": "\\(1-\\frac{3}{e^2}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, \\(\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{r})=\\frac{e^{-\\lambda} \\lambda^r}{r !}\\) (where \\(\\lambda=\\) mean)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n\\therefore \\quad & \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{r} > 1.5)=\\mathrm{P}(2)+\\mathrm{P}(3)+\\ldots \\infty \\\\\n& =1-\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=\\mathrm{r} \\leq 1)=1-\\mathrm{P}(0)-\\mathrm{P}(1) \\\\\n& =1-\\left(e^{-2}+\\frac{e^{-2} \\times 2}{1 !}\\right)=1-\\frac{3}{e^2}\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
